<DocsLayout title="Cloudflare Tunnel setup" description="Prepare the public ingress used by the MyPaaS dashboard and project subdomains.">
<section><p class="overline">Public ingress</p><h2>Create a tunnel</h2><p>Create a Cloudflare Tunnel for the MyPaaS host from the Cloudflare dashboard. MyPaaS runs its own <code>cloudflared</code> container in production, so the value required by the installer is the tunnel credential, not a second independently installed tunnel service.</p><DocMedia title="Create a Cloudflare Tunnel" source="Cloudflare" note="vendor UI · capture pending" placeholder="Capture the current Cloudflare Tunnels screen and the create-tunnel entry point." /></section>
<section><h2>Route the dashboard hostname</h2><p>Add a published application route for the MyPaaS root hostname, for example <code>mypaas.example.com</code>, and send it to the Caddy HTTP service used by the MyPaaS stack.</p><DocMedia title="Root hostname route" source="Cloudflare" note="vendor UI · capture pending" placeholder="Capture the published application route for the MyPaaS dashboard hostname. Do not include unrelated account identifiers." /></section>
<section><h2>Route project subdomains</h2><p>Add the wildcard hostname used by projects, for example <code>*.mypaas.example.com</code>, to the same Caddy service. Caddy remains the internal router that decides whether traffic belongs to the dashboard, API, static release, or an explicitly routed runtime.</p><DocMedia title="Wildcard project route" source="Cloudflare" note="vendor UI · capture pending" placeholder="Capture the wildcard published application route pointing at the same MyPaaS Caddy service." /></section>
<section><h2>Installer handoff</h2><p>Enter the tunnel credential in the MyPaaS install wizard. The production Compose stack starts <code>cloudflared</code> with that credential and routes inbound tunnel traffic to Caddy.</p><aside class="note"><p>The tunnel is an integration edge. Project containers are not exposed directly to the public network by the MyPaaS routing model.</p></aside><p><a href="/docs/installation/">Return to Installation →</a></p></section>
</DocsLayout>
